WEBVTT

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:14.990
"Hokuto City Municipal Bus Stop"

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:21.000
School
Zone
Slow

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:27.730
"Owner's Manual"

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:32.360
Helmet holder

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.280
Here it is.
Helmet holder

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:34.360
Helmet holder

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.870
This must be it.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:55.640
Huh...?

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:12.950
Uh-oh.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.460
Year

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.830
I rode my motorbike to school today!

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:14.670
Huh?!

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.220
Hey, are you serious?

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:18.300
Amazing! When did you get your license?

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.300
What do you ride?

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.470
Show me! Show me!

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:21.850
-What kind of bike is it?
-That's awesome!

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:24.140
Oh, um...

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.550
Pasta again?

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:18.880
Well, I like it.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:23.010
Hey, want to eat with me?

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:25.800
I'm sorry, but there's something
I need to take care of.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.350
Okay. Some other time, then.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:32.770
"Oyakodon"

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:58.050
Okay. Today, I'd like for all of you...
to make a drawstring bag like this one.

00:05:58.050 --> 00:05:59.880
Drawstring bag...?

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:06.470
For the fabric, you are free
to use anything in here.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:09.640
Please follow your textbooks.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:16.520
Wow, how come you're so good?

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.770
Show me how to do it, too!

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:20.280
What kind did you choose?

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:21.570
I got this one.

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:23.740
You sure like that color, don't you?

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:29.540
What are you going to use all that for?
Money must be tight.

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:32.200
Don't tell me you're getting
ready to run away.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:36.130
I was thinking of putting my helmet
and gloves for my motorbike in it.

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:37.880
Huh? You have your license?

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:40.130
For real? What do you ride?

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:42.920
A Super Cub. A used one.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:47.470
Oh, a Cub? That's more of a scooter
than a motorbike, isn't it?

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:49.050
A Cub is that one kind, right?

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:52.350
The one that soba restaurants
and newspapers use for deliveries?

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:00.440
You ride a Cub?

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:02.990
Well, a used one.

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:05.070
Would you mind letting me see it later?

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:06.490
Huh?

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:13.410
Maybe after our classes are over.

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:16.920
Sure. Okay, see you then.

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.370
I didn't get today's math at all.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:59.290
It was hard, all right.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:01.290
I mean, the way she
teaches it is so bad...

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:03.300
That's true.

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.420
Well, what can we do?

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:17.560
Here, you forgot something.

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:21.310
Th-Thanks.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:22.310
Let's give our best today.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.650
Mm-hmm, let's.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.030
This is...

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:29.570
Wow! You have a prime
carburetor-style Cub!

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:35.120
It only has a bit over 500 kilos on it.
Oh, and the tires are still brand new!

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:39.370
Ah, Cubs really are the coolest.

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:45.090
Oh, and you have an Arai Classic helmet.
That's a great match for a Cub.

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:47.630
I use a Shoei Hornet, myself.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:51.840
What about your gloves?
What are you using?

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:55.810
Huh? Oh, let's see...

00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:02.400
Grip Swany, huh?
Mine are non-slip work gloves.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:03.480
Work gloves?

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.860
Yep, work gloves.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:11.110
I ride my motorbike to school, too.

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:12.990
Huh?

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:14.530
Wanna see?

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:17.750
Oh, um...

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.580
Mm-hmm.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:25.130
H-H-Hold on! Hold on a minute, right here!

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:41.850
Huh?

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:45.150
Is that...?

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:50.070
A Honda MD90 Postal Cub.

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:53.280
Like the post office uses.

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:56.370
Yep. From before environmental
and noise regulations

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:59.080
made them scale back the power on these.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:02.620
It's a Cub from before they had electronic
controls worth fiddling with.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:07.290
Steel.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:12.340
I've souped it up a little since I got it,
and gotten it so it goes pretty fast.

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:17.430
The engine parts, the brakes,
and the suspension are all Takegawa.

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:19.720
The muffler is a one-off titanium piece.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:23.730
I had to give them nearly enough to
pay off their office in Tondabayashi.

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:53.220
Whew, it's getting warm.
Sorry for doing all the talking.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:57.760
But I'm glad to meet a fellow Cub rider.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:59.220
See you.

00:11:57.740 --> 00:12:02.530
A girl in my class, whose name and
face are the only things I know...

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:10.880
I wonder if she'll talk to me
again tomorrow, too.

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:19.090
For now, we at least have our Cubs
in common to talk about.

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:31.900
As I recall... her name is...

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:38.070
Reiko
Super Cub
Episode 2

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:10.520
The time is now 7:25.
And now for the weather.

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:15.150
The current temperature around
the area is 19.7 degrees in Kofu,

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:20.280
17.5 degrees at Lake Kawaguchi,
and 18.4 degrees in Tokyo.

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:24.780
Due to a high-pressure system
over the Japanese archipelago,

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:27.370
today's weather for the
Kanto-Koshinetsu region will be sunny.

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:08.160
Good.

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:12.520
Morning.

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:10.280
G-Good morning.

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:11.200
Hmm?

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:12.490
Mm-hmm.

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:50.820
"Gyudon"

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:58.250
Reiko-<i>san</i>, want to eat lunch together?

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:02.380
Sorry, I was planning to have
my lunch today with a friend.

00:17:02.380 --> 00:17:04.670
Oh. Oh, well.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:06.380
Some other time, then.

00:17:18.270 --> 00:17:20.520
All right, let's go.

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:22.100
Huh?

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:24.230
H-Hold on...

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:30.280
Okay, ready to have lunch?

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.620
Together, as friends.

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:45.460
Thank you for this food!

00:17:56.140 --> 00:17:58.560
Sitting on my Cub like this,

00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:01.690
it feels like I can go anywhere
I like, as far away as I like,

00:18:01.690 --> 00:18:05.270
even when I'm standing still.

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:10.820
I haven't gone all that far away, so...

00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:26.750
You can go anywhere you want to.
I mean, you've got a Cub!

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:50.360
Hurry, hurry!

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:51.820
Hey, wait up!

00:18:51.820 --> 00:18:53.360
I'll be cheering for you at your game.

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:55.030
Oh, thank you.

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:56.800
Sitting on my Cub like this,

00:19:56.800 --> 00:19:59.930
it feels like I can go anywhere
I like, as far away as I like,

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:03.560
even when I'm standing still.

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:08.150
I haven't gone all that far away, so...

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:14.530
You can go anywhere you want to.
I mean, you've got a Cub!

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:21.370
I can go anywhere I want to...

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:53.560
Mukawa
Supermarket

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:14.130
That's cheap.

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:23.800
Thank you very much.

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:25.390
Welcome.

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:27.840
2-yen charge for shopping bags

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:29.810
Thank you very much.

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:39.030
Up to now, I haven't gone shopping
on the way home from school,

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:41.530
or anywhere else that much, either.

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:47.240
I turned at an intersection
where I always go straight,

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:50.250
and what I found spread out before me...

00:21:52.960 --> 00:21:55.590
...were unknown places...

00:21:55.590 --> 00:21:57.800
...unknown streets...

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:01.300
...and I'm sure...

00:22:01.300 --> 00:22:03.760
...there are unknown sights to see, too.

00:22:24.490 --> 00:22:24.570
Oh, yeah, my chain lock.

00:22:24.570 --> 00:22:27.990
Komeri
Oh, yeah, my chain lock.

00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:28.070
Komeri

00:22:30.700 --> 00:22:33.040
I'll go there tomorrow.

00:22:41.010 --> 00:22:44.130
Side trips on my Super Cub...

00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:48.560
I'm kind of looking forward
to tomorrow after school.

